**FIRST, for any book work (Step 0, preview, render), from any checkout:** `git fetch origin god-mode`, then
`git show origin/god-mode:scripts/book-start.js | node - --slug=<slug>` (add `--check` to look first) - it creates or resumes
the book's own `../wt-book-<slug>` on CURRENT code; work only there and read THAT worktree's files (full text: CLAUDE.md).

Read `AGENTS.md` (the router) and `docs/AGENT-OPERATING-CONTRACT.md` before any work, then `CLAUDE.md` (strict
invariants that bind every agent). Procedures live once, in `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` — read the file the
router names and follow it; this rule never restates them.

Cursor specifics:
- Production decisions come from commands, not from this text: `node scripts/preview-state.js status --slug=<slug>`
  (next action / stop), `production-guard` refusals (exit 2), one-run locks (exit 3). Follow what they print.
- A "fresh agent" in a procedure is a NEW Cursor agent/chat given only that prompt file. If you cannot start one, stop
  and report — never write and judge the same frames in one context.
- A refused storyboard merge is a work list, not a question: fix every problem yourself by its code
  (`storyboard/merge-report.json`, skill preview-hazirla "Merge recovery"), whatever the count; stop only for OPERATOR.
- The turn never ends on CONTINUE: no "shall I continue?", no interim HAZIR DEĞİL report. It ends only at READY, at an
  OPERATOR stop, or while waiting for agents you started (skill preview-hazirla §2).
